    <tags>korean ime hangul hotkey shift-space keyboard lightweight portable led</tags>
    <summary>nShiftSpace keyboard-LED build: Shift+Space IME toggle whose tray icon lights up while any key is held (6KB)</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
**nShiftSpace LED** is the keyboard-LED build of nShiftSpace (Nexa ShiftSpace), the
ultra-lightweight Windows tray utility that toggles the Korean/English IME with
**Shift+Space**.

Everything the standard `nshiftspace` package does, plus:

- The tray icon turns green while any key is held and back to blue when released -
  a keyboard activity LED in the tray. Uses Raw Input (no keyboard hook, so it never
  delays other programs' key input)
- Tray menu toggle "Keyboard LED" - turning it off unregisters Raw Input, so the
  per-keystroke cost drops to zero like the standard build

Common features: single ~6KB executable, no C runtime, pure Win32 API, zero CPU while
idle, about 0.3MB in Task Manager, "Start at login" tray toggle, single-instance guard.

Install either `nshiftspace` or `nshiftspace-led`, not both - they share the same
hotkey and only one instance runs at a time.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/SosomLab/nexa-shortcut/releases</releaseNotes>
